{
  "dom_id": "step-q75547",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The surface area of a cylinder is given by \n\n$$\nA=2\\pi rh\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.\n\nWhat is the formula for the height of the cylinder in terms of the other variables?",
  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $h,$ so we will treat the other variables $A$ and $r$ as constants.\n\nFirst, we rearrange and then divide both sides by $2\\pi r$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =2\\pi rh \\\\ A & =(2\\pi r)h \\\\ \\frac{A}{2\\pi r} & =\\frac{(2\\pi r)h}{2\\pi r} \\\\ \\frac{A}{2\\pi r} & =h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $h=\\frac{A}{2\\pi r}.$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $r\\ne 0.$",
